YANI: shrubs that grow food, food that grows back
after a few thousand turns post-harvest, for
adventurers who like to forage as they explore.

The fruit or whatever doesn't have to be highly
nourishing, or even non-lethal, but clues to
recognizing the more edible types, descriptions
randomized each game, might show up in fortune
cookie messages (a mix of truth and lies,
naturally), or be purchasable from the Oracle
(slanted toward truths).

Some fruits might have special properties, beyond
the obvious "Montezuma's Revenge Bush"'s crop, such
as improved infravision, more acute hearing,
improved eating capacity, one-use magical breathing
from the fruit of the oxygen berry bush, all of
limited duration or single use, all as subject to
rotting as any foodstuff.

